\title{multiCollglm: collinearity diagnostics for GLMs and glmnet}
\description{
Provides \code{\link[=condition_number]{condition_number()}}, \code{\link[=bkw_diagnostics]{bkw_diagnostics()}} and
\code{\link[=rvif_diagnostics]{rvif_diagnostics()}} to assess collinearity in generalized linear
models. By default they are computed, following Weissfeld and Sereika
(1991), over the design matrix weighted by the IRLS weights at
convergence and scaled to unit length (without centering); the \code{method}
argument also offers the definition of MacKinnon and Puterman (1989),
the one of the original (unweighted) design matrix, and the raw
information matrix.
Works directly on \code{glm} objects, and on \code{glmnet}/\code{cv.glmnet} objects by
internally refitting a \code{glm} on the active set of variables at the
given lambda. \code{\link[=ml_collinearity]{ml_collinearity()}} adds the complementary diagnostic of
Lesaffre and Marx (1993), comparing the condition number of the
original design matrix against that of the IRLS-weighted information
matrix to distinguish ordinary collinearity from ML-collinearity.
